==Battleground==
*1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns as the boss after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*4 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*6 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*6 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 7.67 seconds<sup>230f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*6 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 8.67 seconds<sup>260f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*2 [[Sir Metal Seal]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The waves of Metal enemies can be difficult to fend off, but luckily, they are limited. The stage is practically won once the second Sir Metal Seal is down because all of the Metals will have been exhausted by then. Without any Metals to support him, Kurosawah becomes a sitting duck.

It is also possible to use the Metals as stepping stones for [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]]. Anti-Metal crowd-control helps with this by ensuring a stable frontline. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]] is a great option because of their Area Attack. For wavers, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and Talented [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] are good options, but the former's low DPS means the strategy may take a while if using them. Eventually, Kurosawah should die, leaving only the Metals, which can easily be taken out by [[:Category:Critter-class Cats|Critters]]. If your meatshields are unable to keep up with the Metals' attacks or you don't have enough crowd control units on the field, using slow attack rate critters such as [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] will allow you to thin the horde to a manageable amount without killing all of them to maintain stepping stools to snipe Kurosawah.

Another strategy is to rush the stage, using [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] with Combos to permafreeze Kurosawah during an opening between his attacks, all while still spamming critters to take out the metals, then sending a rusher unit to finish him off before other threats show up. With him gone, your other units should be able to defeat the remaining enemies.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]]: A basic, yet powerful critter for this stage. Their Talents improve them further, increasing their crit chance and cost-efficiency significantly.
*Talented Lollycat: Their ability to slow groups of Metals is handy here, as the Metals can be very threatening without proper crowd-control.
*Talented [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: The [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] [[Cat Combo]] is needed for her to work, but her high-damage crits can destroy any Metals that stack up. Her crit chance remains low even with combos, so she should never be relied on.
*[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]]: They are very effective against the Metal Doges, being able to clear them before they have the chance to chew through your defenses. They also benefit greatly from the aforementioned Miracle Performance combo.
*Waitress Cat: Her strong crits are more than enough to gravely cripple the Sir Metal Seals. Her long attack rate and Single Attack are problems that must be accounted for, however. Hurricat pairs well with her by clearing out the weak peons to guarantee a hit on Sir Metal Seal.
*[[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern/Future Cat]]: Only available on higher crown difficulties, but she is your best meatshield option here by far. Her [[True Form]] just makes her even better at her role.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: A powerful and disposable Waver that can deal serious damage to Kurosawah on higher crown difficulties. Pre-True Form will work, but gets outranged by Sir Metal Seal.

